incentivizing States to enhance educational outcomes. II. 45% of the net proceeds of Union taxes
are to be shared with States. III. ₹ 45,000 crores are to be kept as performance-based incentive
for all States for carrying out agricultural reforms.
IV. It re-introduced tax-effort criteria to reward fiscal performance.
