INSERT INTO prelims_pyqs (exam_year, subject, subtopic, difficulty, question_number, question_text, correct_answer, embedding, search_vector) VALUES (
    2024, 'Economy', 'Banking and Finance', 'moderate', 149,
    'difficult
Q49. With reference to the rule/rules imposed by the Reserve Bank of India while treating foreign
banks, consider the following statements :
1. There is no minimum capital requirement for wholly owned banking subsidiaries in India.
2. For wholly owned banking subsidiaries in India, at least 50% of the board members should be
Indian nationals.
Which of the statements given above is/are correct ?
(a) 1 only
