    to_tsvector('english', 'Indian Polity ' || 'Parliament & State Legislatures ' || 'With reference to the Parliament of India, consider the following statements :
1. Prorogation of a House by the President of India does not require the advice of the Council of
Ministers.
2. Prorogation of a House is generally done after the House is adjourned sine die but there is no
bar to the President of India prorogating the House which is in session.
3. Dissolution of the Lok Sabha is done by the President of India who, save in exceptional
circumstances, does so on the advice of the Council of Ministers.
Which of the statements given above is/are correct?
(a) 1 only
(b) 1 and 2
(c) 2 and 3
(d) 3 only')
);

