INSERT INTO prelims_pyqs (exam_year, subject, subtopic, difficulty, question_number, question_text, correct_answer, embedding, search_vector) VALUES (
    2023, 'Indian Economy', 'Financial Markets & Capital Markets', 'moderate', 221,
    'difficult
Q21. Consider the following statements:
Statement-I:
Interest income from the deposits in Infrastructure Investment Trusts (InvITs) distributed to
their investors is exempted from tax, but the dividend is taxable.
Statement-II:
InvITs are recognized as borrowers under the ''Securitization and Reconstruction of Financial
Assets and Enforcement of Security Interest Act, 2002''.
Which one of the following is correct in respect of the above statements?
(a) Both Statement-I and Statement-II are correct and Statement-II is the correct explanation for
Statement-I
(b) Both Statement-I and Statement-II are correct and Statement-II is not the correct explanation for
