INSERT INTO prelims_pyqs (exam_year, subject, subtopic, difficulty, question_number, question_text, correct_answer, embedding, search_vector) VALUES (
    2021, 'Environment & Ecology', 'Sustainable Agriculture & Forestry', 'moderate', 451,
    'difficult
Q51. How is permaculture farming different from conventional chemical farming?
1. Permaculture farming discourages monocultural practices but in conventional chemical
farming, monoculture practices are pre- dominant.
2. Conventional chemical farming can cause increase in soil salinity but the occurrence of such
phenomenon is not observed in permaculture farming.
3. Conventional chemical farming is easily possible in semi-arid regions but permaculture farming
is not so easily possible in such regions.
4. Practice of mulching is very important in permaculture farming but not necessarily so in
conventional chemical farming.
Select the correct answer using the code given below.
(a) 1 and 3
