    to_tsvector('english', 'Indian Polity ' || 'Constitutional Framework & Development ' || 'Consider the following statements :
1. The 44th Amendment to the Constitution of India introduced an Article placing the election of
the Prime Minister beyond judicial review.
2. The Supreme Court of India struck down the 99th Amendment to the Constitution of India as
being violative of the independence of judiciary.
