    to_tsvector('english', 'Environment & Ecology ' || 'Environmental Governance & Legislation ' || 'In India, if a species of tortoise is declared protected under Schedule I of the Wild Life
(Protection) Act, 1972, what does it imply?
(a) It enjoys the same level of protection as the tiger.
(b) It no longer exists in the wild, a few individuals are under captive protection; and now it is impossible to
prevent its extinction.
(c) It is endemic to a particular region of India.
(d) Both (b) and (c) stated above are correct in this context.')
);

