INSERT INTO prelims_pyqs (exam_year, subject, subtopic, difficulty, question_number, question_text, correct_answer, embedding, search_vector) VALUES (
    2014, 'Art & Culture', 'Sculpture & Iconography', 'moderate', 85,
    'With reference to the Indian history of art and culture, consider the following pairs: Famous
work of sculpture — Site
1. A grand image of Buddha’s Mahaparinirvana with numerous celestial musicians above and the
sorrowful figures of his followers below — Ajanta
2. A huge image of Varaha Avatar (boar incarnation) of Vishnu, as he rescues Goddess Earth from
the deep and chaotic waters, sculpted on rock — Mount Abu
3. “Arjuna’s Penance” / “Descent of Ganga” sculpted on the surface of huge boulders —
Mamallapuram
Which of the pairs given above is/are correctly matched?
(a) 1 and 2 only
