2. DRDAs undertake area-specific scientific study of the causes of poverty and malnutrition and
prepare detailed remedial measures.
3. DRDAs secure inter-sectoral and inter-departmental coordination and cooperation for effective
implementation of anti-poverty programmes.
4. DRDAs watch over and ensure effective utilization of the funds intended for anti-poverty
programmes.
