    to_tsvector('english', 'Current Affairs ' || 'International Organisations & Groupings ' || 'difficult
Q49. Recently, the USA decided to support India''s membership in multi-lateral export control
regimes called the "Australia Group" and the "Wassenaar Arrangement". What is the difference
between them?
1. The Australia Group is an informal arrangement which aims to allow exporting countries to
minimize the risk of assisting chemical and biological weapons proliferation, whereas the
Wassenaar Arrangement is a formal group under the OECD holding identical objectives.
2. The Australia Group comprises predominantly of Asian, African and North American countries,
whereas the member countries of Wassenaar Arrangement are predominantly from the
European Union and American continents.
Which of the statements given above is/are correct ?
(a) 1 only
(b) 2 only
(c) Both 1 and 2
(d) Neither 1 nor 2')
);

