    to_tsvector('english', 'Geography ' || 'Indian Physical Geography ' || 'difficult
Q97. The Brahmaputra, Irrawady and Mekong rivers originate in Tibet and flow through narrow
and parallel mountain ranges in their upper reaches. Of these rivers, Brahmaputra makes a "U"
turn in its course to flow into India. This "U" turn is due to
(a) uplift of folded Himalayan series
(b) syntaxis bending of geologically young Himalayas
(c) geo-tectonic disturbance in the tertiary folded mountain chains
(d) Both (a) and (b) above')
);

