1. The sum of the number of persons who take either tea or coffee or both is four times the
number of persons who take both coffee and tea.
2. The sum of the number of persons who take only coffee and those who take only tea is twice
the number of persons who take both coffee and tea.
Which of the statements given above is/are correct?
