INSERT INTO prelims_pyqs (exam_year, subject, subtopic, difficulty, question_number, question_text, correct_answer, embedding, search_vector) VALUES (
    1999, 'Science & Technology', 'Quantitative Aptitude', 'moderate', 146,
    'In an office, the distribution of work hours is as shown in the following table:
No. of Staff Members | No. of hours worked
5  | 0 – 19
12 | 20 – 24
25 | 25 – 29
40 | 30 – 34
15 | 35 – 39
8  | 40 – 45
Consider the following inferences drawn from the table:
I. The average number of hours worked by a staff member is about 30.
II. The percentage of those who worked 35 or more hours is less than 25.
III. At least 5 staff members worked more than 44 hours.
Which of these inferences is/are valid?
(a) I alone
